基于 Jev 聊天助手（https://github.com/jev-chat/jev-chat-jarvis）二次开发。
Built on Jev Chat Assistant (https://github.com/jev-chat/jev-chat-jarvis and
https://github.com/jev-chat/jev-chat-jarvis-mac), MIT. Laya-Heart is an independent
project; it is not made, endorsed or supported by the Jev Chat Assistant authors, by
TypeSafe, by Convai Innovations or by Google. Their LICENSE and NOTICE files are kept in
third_party/.

This product includes:
- laya-ts runtime and export script from Laya (https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya),
  Copyright Convai Innovations, Apache License 2.0 (vendor/laya-ts/LICENSE).
- Laya-Heart's fine-tune (v3) of the Laya-multilingual checkpoint
  (https://huggingface.co/convaiinnovations/laya, subfolder "multilingual"),
  Apache License 2.0, whose encoder is fine-tuned from jhu-clsp/mmBERT-base (MIT), as ONNX.
  It is published on Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/YunkunSong/laya-heart-laya-onnx,
  folder "v3") with both licenses and a NOTICE, and downloaded from there on first start.
  The unchanged ONNX conversion is in the same repository (folder "zero-shot") and the
  release asset "laya-onnx-v1" of this project; see models/README.md.
- onnxruntime-node (Microsoft, MIT).

Laya-Heart does not ship Gemma, llama.cpp or Node.js. On first start, when the user presses
Download, it fetches onto the user's computer Laya-Heart's fine-tune (v4) of Google's Gemma 4
E2B (Apache License 2.0) as a GGUF from Hugging Face
(https://huggingface.co/YunkunSong/laya-heart-gemma-e2b-v4-GGUF) and the official llama.cpp
llama-server build (MIT) from its GitHub
releases; the start scripts fetch Node.js (MIT) from nodejs.org only when the computer has
no Node.js 22 or newer. With Ollama installed, its gemma4:e2b model and the llama-server it
ships (MIT) can be used instead.
